OL,3,GNEWSAWettest week for two years after
OL,4,Anamed storms
OL,5,
OL,6,FEngland had its wettest week for two
OL,7,Fyears, due to heavy rain from two named
OL,8,Fstorms, Austen and Boelo.
OL,10,FThe Environment Agency said the period
OL,11,Fbetween 20 to 27 October was the
OL,12,Fwettest week since October 2024.
OL,14,FA daily average of 55mm of rain fell
OL,15,Facross England in the seven days with
OL,16,Fas much as 87mm in the South West.
OL,18,FMuch of the country remains officially
OL,19,Fin drought, with a severe drought in
OL,20,Fplace across parts of Cornwall, Devon,
OL,21,FDorset, Somerset, East Sussex and West
OL,22,FSussex.
OL,23,APub: 29-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
